message (since `agent.run()` will add it)\n3. **Pass correct user input**: Call 
`agent.run()` with the extracted last user message content\n4. **Applied to both
endpoints**: Fixed both regular (`/completions`) and streaming 
(`/completions/stream`) endpoints\n\n**Implementation Details**:\n- The fix 
handles the conversation history correctly by:\n  - Finding the last user 
message index\n  - Setting `agent.messages` to all messages before that index\n 
- Passing the last user message content to `agent.run()`\n- This matches the 
expected behavior where the API receives full conversation history and needs to 
respond to the last user message\n- The agent\'s `run()` method will add the 
user input to its message history, completing the conversation 
context\n\n**Impact**:\n- API endpoints now correctly process conversation 
history\n- Agents receive the proper context and user input\n- Fixes a critical 
bug where agents were responding to empty prompts\n- Maintains compatibility 
with OpenAI-style chat completion API\n\n**Testing**:\n- Existing tests continue
to pass (except one unrelated test failure in context command)\n- The changes 
are backward compatible with the API interface\n- No breaking changes to API 
request/response format\n\n**Next Steps**:\n1. Consider adding edge case 
handling (e.g., when there\'s no user message in history)\n2. Add comprehensive 
tests for the API endpoints\n3. Consider adding validation for message roles and
structure\n4. Document the API behavior for conversation history handling'})

