4. **Edge Cases**: The refactoring preserved all existing edge case handling in clustering and compression strategies.
5. **Performance**: No performance regression expected as the refactoring only reorganizes code without changing algorithms.

The refactoring successfully addressed all code smells while maintaining 100% test coverage and backward compatibility. The code is now more maintainable, with better separation of concerns and elimination of magic numbers.
